# Quicksave — post-crash recovery orientation (no mid-work lost)
_Printed: 2026-10-10_

## Current task
There is no unfinished work here. The computer crashed with this repo clean except for two
local commits that had never been pushed to `origin/main`. Both are now pushed. This quicksave
exists purely so a fresh session typing "do" or "recover" gets real orientation instead of
"nothing to restore."

## Decisions locked this session
- Pushed `main` to `origin/main` (was ahead by 2 commits — `2cf530a` and `992a5bc`).
- This repo already had the quicksave/quickload RECOVER trio (`.claude\commands\quicksave.md`,
  `.claude\commands\quickload.md`, `.claude\hooks\quickload-on-do.ps1`), byte-identical to the
  ChiMesh template. Extended the hook's trigger regex from `(do|do it)` to
  `(do|do it|recover)` so typing "recover" works identically to "do". Matching prose mentions of
  "do" in all three files now also say "do" or "recover".

